prepare-storage-roots-from-project-directory

Lane: cross

Unit: configure-workspace-roots-from-project-directory

ChildPatch: prepare-storage-roots-from-project-directory

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Configure the cwd-derived local Workspace across startup, resume and accepted directory changes.

Requires: Unit:normalization/normalize-base-roots-for-processes, FlatPatch:normalization/initialize-tmpdir-before-process-startup, FlatPatch:backend/persist-thread-settings-without-runtime

Provides: Prepare six selected roots and scratch language directories; bind their inherited values, seven-tree Workspace write access and nonrecursive shell-policy root references to the current local cwd at local execution boundaries; preserve canonical thread profiles, captured environments and native constraints; suppress only cwd control discovery when its AGENTS.override.md is empty.

Boundary: Base roots and TMPDIR remain normalization-owned. Approval, network policy, named custom profiles and owner-provided environments retain native ownership. Remote execution never prepares host project roots. Shell templates remain raw until local preparation and invalid references fail that environment. Ancestor, user, system, plugin and explicit skill roots remain discoverable.

Verification: Core tests cover root defaults and overrides, canonical profile preservation, cwd rebinding, constraints, failures, shell-reference syntax, remote inheritance and snapshot isolation. App-server and TUI tests cover start, resume, settings, standalone commands and /cd. Shell, hook, Guardian and MCP tests cover filtering and captured-environment reuse; loader and skill-root tests cover empty overrides and preserved ancestor controls.

CrossGroup: workspace-permissions


